Should we fail here when `kv_cache_layout` is `None`? Silently omitting it recreates the old namespace and could bring this bug back if layout propagation ever regresses. Since this value should already be resolved at this point, I think the direct path should require it.

```suggestion
        if canonical_format is not None:
            self.fields["canonical_format"] = canonical_format
        else:
            if kv_cache_layout is None:
                raise ValueError("KV cache layout has not been resolved")
            self.fields["kv_cache_layout"] = kv_cache_layout
```

It would be good to add a small test covering this failure case.

